# Two Twists and Turns (CR 614.5, 616.1, the ruling): each replacement effect applies to the explore once, so "a creature you control would explore" gets
# "instead you scry 1, then that creature explores" twice over - scry 1, scry 1 again, then the one explore, not two. The second Twists and Turns' own enters trigger, which
# targets the Ornithopter, is the explore: Bot1 scries the Lightning Bolt to the bottom, then Mox Jet to the bottom, and the Ornithopter explores the Forest beneath them.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Forest
Ornithopter
Twists and Turns
Twists and Turns
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt
Mox Jet
Forest
Mountain
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Twists and Turns.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Twists and Turns.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Arrange( | Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Arrange( | Mox Jet)

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Island; Island
Bot1.Library.Count = 15
Bot1.Library.Top = Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
